From beac9bd4235fae4faf8efbc90188923cdf2ab735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:42:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] um: arm64: support loadable modules

aarch64 modules are RELA and need apply_relocate_add(), PLT veneers for
branches out of range, and the immediate-field encoders that write the
relocated instructions. None of that is a property of how the kernel is
hosted -- it is the aarch64 ELF ABI and the instruction set -- so this
reuses arch/arm64/kernel/module.c and module-plts.c rather than growing a
second copy that would have to be kept in step forever. x86 UML has taken
exactly that approach to its own module.c for years.

What has to be supplied locally is small: the relocation constants,
arm64's struct mod_arch_specific and module linker script (which a
generic-y wrapper in arch/um would otherwise shadow, since generated
headers win the include path), and aarch64_insn_copy(). arch/arm64's
version of the last one manufactures a writable alias of read-only kernel
text; a UML guest has no such mapping, so this one is a memcpy plus the
I-cache maintenance a real CPU still requires.

The headers that arch/arm64/kernel/module.c reaches for on the way --
alternative.h, cpufeature.h, debug-monitors.h, kprobes.h, simd.h -- are
stubs here, because the features behind them are properties of a CPU this
kernel does not drive.

MODULES_USE_ELF_RELA is now selected, having been deliberately left out
while nothing implemented apply_relocate_add().

Signed-off-by: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/module-plts.c    |   9 +++
 arch/arm64/lib/insn.c              |   1 +
 arch/arm64/um/Kconfig              |  13 ++--
 arch/arm64/um/Makefile             |  19 ++++-
 arch/arm64/um/asm/alternative.h    |  32 ++++++++
 arch/arm64/um/asm/cpufeature.h     |  33 +++++++++
 arch/arm64/um/asm/debug-monitors.h |  15 ++++
 arch/arm64/um/asm/elf.h            |  42 ++++++++++-
 arch/arm64/um/asm/kprobes.h        |  18 +++++
 arch/arm64/um/asm/module.h         | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/um/asm/module.lds.h     |  27 +++++++
 arch/arm64/um/asm/simd.h           |  28 +++++++
 arch/arm64/um/patching.c           |  45 ++++++++++++
 arch/um/include/asm/Kbuild         |   7 ++
 arch/um/os-Linux/user_syms.c       |  19 ++++-
 15 files changed, 414 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/um/asm/alternative.h
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/um/asm/cpufeature.h
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/um/asm/debug-monitors.h
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/um/asm/kprobes.h
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/um/asm/module.h
